# ############################################################################
# !!!  PLACEHOLDER OWNERS - CODE-OWNER REVIEW IS NOT ENFORCED YET  !!!
# Every @your-org/* team below is a placeholder. Until they are replaced with
# real teams, GitHub silently ignores these lines and NO code-owner review is
# required for any path (including IAM, KMS, org policy and CI).
# The "CODEOWNERS placeholders" job in terraform-plan.yml warns on every run;
# set the repository variable CODEOWNERS_ENFORCE=true after replacing them so
# a placeholder reappearing fails CI (docs/guides/CI_SECRETS.md).
# ############################################################################
#
# CODEOWNERS — team ownership for the landing zone (audit L / bus-factor).
#
# ACTION REQUIRED: replace every @your-org/* placeholder below with your real
# GitHub teams. This scaffold is INERT until all of the following are true:
#   1. The teams exist and each has at least one member.
#   2. Branch protection on the default branch has "Require review from Code
#      Owners" enabled (docs/guides/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md).
#   3. The required teams together have at least two people, so a guardrail change
#      cannot be self-approved. The previous single-owner file made the
#      "CODEOWNERS review + 1 approval" gate a bus-factor of one; team ownership
#      with a distinct security team removes that.
#
# The current maintainer should join @your-org/platform-team (and the security
# team) rather than being named here, so ownership survives one person leaving.
#
# PRECEDENCE: GitHub applies the LAST matching line only, and every owner on that
# line is required. General areas are listed first; security-sensitive paths come
# LATER so they win and require BOTH the platform and the security team. Keep that
# order when editing.

# ── Default ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
* @your-org/platform-team

# ── CI/CD, supply-chain, and security gates ──────────────────────────────────
# The scanners and the pipeline are a security control, so the security team is
# a required reviewer alongside platform.
/.github/                 @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/scripts/                 @your-org/platform-team
/Makefile                 @your-org/platform-team
/.terraform-docs.yml      @your-org/platform-team
/.tflint.hcl              @your-org/platform-team
/.checkov.yaml            @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/.pre-commit-config.yaml  @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team

# ── Deployable roots ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/envs/           @your-org/platform-team
/envs/saas/      @your-org/app-platform-team

# ── Modules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/modules/gcp/        @your-org/platform-team
/modules/aws/        @your-org/platform-team
/modules/tfc/        @your-org/platform-team
/modules/supabase/   @your-org/app-platform-team
/modules/vercel/     @your-org/app-platform-team
/modules/saas/       @your-org/app-platform-team

# ── Examples and docs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/examples/     @your-org/platform-team
/docs/         @your-org/docs-team
SECURITY.md    @your-org/security-team
CHANGELOG.md   @your-org/platform-team

# ── Control-plane and security roots (platform + security REQUIRED) ──────────
# Listed after the general /envs/ line so they take precedence. A change to the
# org structure, guardrails, audit logging, the TFC workspace layer, or the
# identity plane needs a second, security-team approval.
/envs/gcp/bootstrap/      @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/gcp/organization/   @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/aws/organization/   @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/aws/security/       @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/aws/identity/       @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/aws/backup/         @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/envs/tfc-admin/          @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team

# ── Security-sensitive modules (platform + security REQUIRED) ────────────────
# IAM, governance/guardrails, KMS, deny policies, break-glass, and the whole AWS
# security baseline. Listed after the general /modules/ lines so they win.
/modules/gcp/governance/  @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/gcp/iam/         @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/aws/governance/  @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/aws/iam/         @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
/modules/aws/security/    @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team

# ── This file ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Changing ownership itself needs both teams.
/.github/CODEOWNERS  @your-org/platform-team @your-org/security-team
